## ✅ Modern React + TypeScript Rules for Cursor and Claude Code

### 🔠 **Component Typing**

* **DO NOT use `React.FC`**

  ❌ `const MyComponent: React.FC<Props> = () => { ... }`
  ✅ `function MyComponent(props: Props) { ... }`
  ✅ `const MyComponent = (props: Props) => { ... }`

  > Avoid `React.FC` because it:
  >
  > * Implicitly adds `children`, even if not expected.
  > * Obscures prop types in editors/hover tooltips.
  > * Makes defaultProps harder to use with TypeScript.

---

### 🧱 **Props & Types**

* **Always type the `props` object explicitly**

  ✅ Define a `Props` type or inline it:

  ```ts
  type Props = { title: string; };
  const Header = ({ title }: Props) => <h1>{title}</h1>;
  ```

* **Group and name prop types clearly**

  ✅ `interface ButtonProps` or `type ButtonProps` — use `Props` suffix.

* **Use `interface` for public/shared components; `type` for local-only**

  > `interface` is preferred when extending, especially in component libraries.

* **Prefer union types over enums**

  ✅

  ```ts
  type Geography =
    | "Australia"
    | "United States";
  ```

  ❌

  ```ts
  enum Geography {
    AU = "Australia",
    US = "United States",
  }
  ```

---

### 🔁 **Hooks & State**

* **Always type hook return values if reused/shared**

  ✅

  ```ts
  function useUser(): [User | null, boolean] {
    ...
  }
  ```

* **Avoid excessive `useEffect` for derived state**

  > Use memoization or derived variables instead of syncing with effects.

---

### 📦 **Component Structure**

* **One component per file** (unless small and tightly coupled)
* **Use PascalCase** for file and component names: `UserCard.tsx`, `MyForm.tsx`
* **Group hooks and utilities into folders**: `/hooks`, `/utils`, `/components`
* **Presentation-layer components**: `/components/ui`

---

### 📐 **Zod Schemas**

* **Use the same name for schemas and inferred types**
* **Use upper camel case for names**
* **Avoid `Schema` and `Type` suffix in names**
* **Prefer readable code over excessive comments**

---

### 🎨 **Styling**

* Use Tailwind CSS for app styling.
* Control style of Tracksuit Design components by adding Tailwind classes.
* Avoid global or custom CSS.

---

### 🧪 **Testing & Storybook**

* Co-locate test files: `MyComponent.test.tsx`
* Use Testing Library; avoid low-level DOM inspection.
* Use User Events instead of `fireEvent`.
* Avoid [common mistakes with React Testing Library](https://kentcdodds.com/blog/common-mistakes-with-react-testing-library)

---

### 🤖 **AI Collaboration Optimizations (for Cursor & Claude)**

* **Use named exports over default exports**

  ✅ `export const Button = () => ...`
  ❌ `export default () => ...`

* **Always place `export` statements at the end of the file**

  ✅

  ```ts
  const Button = () => { ... };
  export { Button };
  ```

  ❌

  ```ts
  export const Button = () => { ... };
  ```

  > This helps AI tools like Cursor and Claude understand full context before exports, improving autocomplete, inlining, and code navigation.

* **Keep components small and composable** — improves refactorability.

* **Use clear function and type names for improved suggestions**

* **Comment non-obvious components or logic with short doc-style comments**

  ✅

  ```ts
  // Renders user avatar with fallback initials
  const Avatar = ({ user }: AvatarProps) => ...
  ```

---

### 🧼 Miscellaneous

* **Avoid `any`, prefer `unknown` or precise types**

* **Always prefer `key` with stable values** in `.map()`:

  ```ts
  items.map((item) => <Row key={item.id} ... />)
  ```

* **Don’t mix default + named exports in same file** – confuses tooling and AI.
